  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Bank Trade Facilitation Facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of the Trade Facilitation Facility is to expand the capacity of developing countries to implement trade facilitation activities that will lead to the reduction in trade costs to facilitate integration of developing countries into the World Economy.Countries and regional bodies improve trade procedures and regulation, including for women traders and make sound investments and use of trade-related infrastructure.Profile of trade facilitation in development agenda is raised at global, regional and country levels.Sustainable coalitions of  motivated key government agencies are formed and the private sector support trade facilitation in target countries.Global networks of practitioners support the trade facilitation agenda.Support poverty reduction and the Millennium Development Goals by contributing to conditions for sustainable growth in low-income countries</narrative>
  </description>
